E AX3144 1507-field-effect-declaration.ax:8:4-9 field-effect-declaration "the field `count` declares its effects but holds `Int`, which is not a function type" #"declaration not read" !"an effect declaration describes the functions a field holds, so it needs an arrow type such as `(-> Int Int)`" ?"a function-typed field declares `;@axiom:effect(pure)`, or one line per effect its functions may perform: `io`, `alloc`, `mut`, `spawn`, `block`, `entropy` or a declared effect"
E AX3144 1507-field-effect-declaration.ax:10:4-7 field-effect-declaration "`effect(unsafe)` on the field `raw` names no effect a field can declare" #"declaration not read" !"`effect(unsafe)` marks a trusted function; each function a field holds keeps its own unsafe boundary" ?"a function-typed field declares `;@axiom:effect(pure)`, or one line per effect its functions may perform: `io`, `alloc`, `mut`, `spawn`, `block`, `entropy` or a declared effect"
E AX3144 1507-field-effect-declaration.ax:13:4-8 field-effect-declaration "the field `both` declares `effect(pure)` beside another effect" #"declaration not read" !"`effect(pure)` says the field's functions perform nothing; keep it alone, or drop it and list the effects they may perform" ?"a function-typed field declares `;@axiom:effect(pure)`, or one line per effect its functions may perform: `io`, `alloc`, `mut`, `spawn`, `block`, `entropy` or a declared effect"
E AX3144 1507-field-effect-declaration.ax:15:4-7 field-effect-declaration "`effect(teleport)` on the field `far` names no effect a field can declare" #"declaration not read" !"no effect named `teleport` is declared" ?"a function-typed field declares `;@axiom:effect(pure)`, or one line per effect its functions may perform: `io`, `alloc`, `mut`, `spawn`, `block`, `entropy` or a declared effect"
E AX3076 1507-field-effect-declaration.ax:17:4-10 effect-tag-list "`effect(io, alloc)` on `listed` names 2 effects, and an `effect(...)` tag names one" #"one effect per `effect(...)` tag" !"a list here was read as ONE effect spelled with the comma in it, which nothing declares - so the claim could never be satisfied, and AX3010 reported it missing from a body that performed it. `restrict(...)` takes a comma list; `effect(...)` does not" ?"write one tag line per effect: `;@axiom:effect(io)` and `;@axiom:effect(alloc)`"
E AX3077 1507-field-effect-declaration.ax:19:4-11 axtag-misplaced "the `restrict` tag on `limited` is never checked: it is a struct field, which takes only `effect(...)`" #"tag not checked here" !"the tag was recorded and nothing read it, so the claim it looks like was never made; an unrecognised key is still legal metadata" ?"a checked claim belongs above the function it describes - its `(:: ...)` or its `(fn ...)`; move it there, or drop it"
E AX3039 1507-field-effect-declaration.ax:21:4-11 axtag-key-typo "AXTAG key typo on `slipped`: unrecognised key `efect`; did you mean `effect`?" ?"an unrecognised key is recorded and never checked, so the claim this looks like was not made. Fix the spelling, or namespace a key of your own, such as `;@axiom:my:KEY(...)`, so it cannot be mistaken for a claim"
